---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="SMS Terms of Service — Army Pink" description="Army Pink SMS Terms of Service — message frequency, opt-out, message and data rates, and TCPA compliance.">

  <div class="legal-layout container">

    <!-- LEFT: STICKY SIDEBAR -->
    <aside class="legal-sidebar" aria-label="SMS Terms sections">
      <nav class="legal-nav">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#program" data-section-link>Program description</a></li>
          <li><a href="#consent" data-section-link>Consent</a></li>
          <li><a href="#frequency" data-section-link>Message frequency</a></li>
          <li><a href="#rates" data-section-link>Message and data rates</a></li>
          <li><a href="#opt-out" data-section-link>How to opt out</a></li>
          <li><a href="#help" data-section-link>How to get help</a></li>
          <li><a href="#privacy" data-section-link>Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="#carriers" data-section-link>Supported carriers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes" data-section-link>Changes to these terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contact" data-section-link>Contact us</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <!-- RIGHT: CONTENT -->
    <article class="legal-content">

      <header class="legal-header">
        <h1>SMS Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: May 22, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; TCPA compatible</p>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          How Army Pink's text messaging program works, and how you can opt out at any time.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- §1 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="program">
        <h2>1. Program description</h2>
        <p>
          Army Pink's SMS program delivers messages directly related to your safe
          transportation rides and wellness support services — including appointment
          confirmations, ride coordination, and program updates you've requested.
        </p>
        <p>
          Messages are transmitted through our delivery provider, <strong>Twilio,
          Inc.</strong>, under a data processing agreement limiting Twilio's use of
          your information solely to message delivery.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §2 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="consent">
        <h2>2. Consent</h2>
        <p>
          By providing your phone number and confirming consent, you agree to receive
          SMS messages from Army Pink. Providing your phone number and consenting to
          receive SMS messages is <strong>not a condition of eligibility</strong> for
          Army Pink services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §3 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="frequency">
        <h2>3. Message frequency</h2>
        <p>
          Message frequency varies based on your service appointments and the support
          you've requested. You will not receive marketing or promotional messages
          unless you've separately opted in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §4 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="rates">
        <h2>4. Message and data rates</h2>
        <p>
          Message and data rates may apply, depending on your mobile carrier and
          service plan. Army Pink does not charge for messages — any cost is set by
          your carrier.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §5 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="opt-out">
        <h2>5. How to opt out</h2>
        <p>
          You may revoke consent and opt out at any time by texting
          <strong>STOP</strong> to any Army Pink message. You will receive one final
          confirmation message, and no further messages will be sent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Opting out will not affect your access to services.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          To resume receiving messages after opting out, text <strong>START</strong>
          to any Army Pink number you previously received messages from, or contact
          us directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §6 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="help">
        <h2>6. How to get help</h2>
        <p>For support with our SMS program:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Text <strong>HELP</strong> to any Army Pink message</li>
          <li>Email <a href="mailto:support@armypink.org">support@armypink.org</a></li>
          <li>Call <a href="tel:12135795051">(213) 579-5051</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- §7 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="privacy">
        <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Your phone number and any personally identifying information collected in
          connection with our SMS program will not be sold, rented, or disclosed to any
          third party, except as described in our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §8 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="carriers">
        <h2>8. Supported carriers</h2>
        <p>
          Army Pink's SMS program is compatible with major U.S. wireless carriers,
          including AT&amp;T, Verizon, T-Mobile, and Sprint, as well as their regional
          affiliates. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §9 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="changes">
        <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. When we make material changes,
          we will update the "last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use
          of our SMS program after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §10 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="contact">
        <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
        <address class="privacy-contact">
          <strong>Army Pink</strong><br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:support@armypink.org">support@armypink.org</a><br>
          Phone: <a href="tel:12135795051">(213) 579-5051</a>
        </address>
      </section>

    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- Sticky sidebar active-section highlight -->
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var links = document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-link]');
      if (!links.length) return;
      var sections = Array.from(links).map(function (a) {
        return document.querySelector(a.getAttribute('href'));
      }).filter(Boolean);

      function setActive(id) {
        links.forEach(function (a) {
          a.classList.toggle('is-active', a.getAttribute('href') === '#' + id);
        });
      }

      var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        var visible = entries
          .filter(function (e) { return e.isIntersecting; })
          .sort(function (a, b) { return a.boundingClientRect.top - b.boundingClientRect.top; });
        if (visible[0]) setActive(visible[0].target.id);
      }, {
        rootMargin: '-100px 0px -60% 0px',
        threshold: 0
      });

      sections.forEach(function (s) { observer.observe(s); });
      if (sections[0]) setActive(sections[0].id);
    })();
  </script>

</Layout>
